{
  "result": "If I could change the world in just one way, I'd give everyone radical empathy \u2014 the ability to truly feel what it's like to walk in someone else's shoes for a moment.\n\nNot to make us all agree, but to make us truly understand each other. So much of the hurt in the world \u2014 arguments, division, cruelty, loneliness \u2014 comes from not being able to see past our own perspective.\n\nI talk to people from all over, with completely different lives and beliefs, and underneath it all most people want the same things: to be safe, to be heard, to matter to someone. I think if we could *feel* that in each other automatically, we'd still have big problems to solve, but we'd solve them *together* instead of against each other.\n\nThat's my magic-wand wish. Curiosity over judgment, understanding over assumption.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 what would *you* change?",
